      ],
      "speedScale": { "slowStroll": 0.7, "default": 1.0, "briskWalk": 1.2 },
      "notes": [
        "contact = heel strike, down = lowest point as weight lands, passing = swing leg moves past stance leg, up = highest point with swing leg reaching forward.",
        "Knee bend: about 5 deg at contact, 15-20 deg on the front leg at down, 30-40 deg on the trailing leg at down, 55-65 deg on the swing leg at passing, 30-40 deg at up.",
        "Stance leg straightens at passing and stays nearly straight through up. A walk never has the deep tuck of a run.",
        "Pelvis is highest over the stance leg at passing or up and lowest at down.",
        "Elbow stays bent a roughly constant 25-35 deg. Arm swing is much smaller than in a run.",
        "Foot rolls heel to toe during down: heel leads at contact, toe trails at the back of the stride."
      ],
